# Line endings.
#
# Fixtures carry digests computed over their raw bytes, so a CRLF conversion on
# checkout changes the bytes and breaks verification: the seed manifest went
# from 526 to 540 bytes on a Windows checkout and its sha256 no longer matched
# the value recorded in tests and shared with the host lane.
#
# `-text` disables all newline translation for these paths, so the bytes on
# disk are the bytes that were committed, on every platform.
fixtures/** -text

# The marketplace plugins are compared byte for byte with what facet bundle
# projects (internal/bundle TestCommittedPluginsMatchThisFacet), and the CLIs
# that clone them read their manifests and digests as committed.
plugins/** -text

*.sh text eol=lf
installer/*.tsv text eol=lf
